                <pb facs="0592" n="580" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg580"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.24/349: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico
                                City</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-03-30T13:00:00-06:00">March 30, 1937—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:13 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>79. The American Consul at Vera Cruz reports that the Spanish ship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Motomar</hi> has been loading airplanes from Tejeria
                    Field since March 27th. The <hi rendition="#italic">Motomar</hi> has left today
                    for Tampico to transport about 500 agrarians and take on oil expecting to return
                    to Vera Cruz to finish loading. All airplanes at Tejeria are reported to be of
                    American manufacture.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
